 "phrases": [
  "Wait. Time just stopped. Because in this split second, your phone does something wild.",
  "It never sends your real card number. Not to the store. Not even to Apple.",
  "So what does it send? Let's go inside.",
  "When you added your card, your bank created a stand-in number. Just for this phone.",
  "It's locked in a tiny vault chip, called the Secure Element.",
  "Even the phone's own software can't read it.",
  "But the vault won't open by itself. First, it needs your face.",
  "Face matched. The vault opens.",
  "Out comes the stand-in number, plus a one-time code made just for this payment.",
  "The reader carries it across. A few centimeters. A fraction of a second.",
  "Only your bank and the card network can match it to your real card.",
  "Approved.",
  "So if a hacker steals that number from the store? Useless. It only works with your phone.",
  "Your real card number never left your pocket.",
  "Pop quiz: what happens to that stand-in number if you lose your phone? Comment below.",
  "Follow Tech Unseen. Next lesson: is your phone secretly listening to you?"
